e</button>\n</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content active\" data-tab=\"HTML\">\n<h2>Most Unifying Text</h2>\n<p><strong>Consensus Score:</strong> 86.51</p>\n<pre><code>To support energy independence and a healthier environment, a revenue-neutral framework can encourage the development of cleaner energy sources. By returning revenue directly to households to protect family budgets and fostering a level playing field for private-sector innovation, we can promote technological growth and economic resilience for all communities.\n</code></pre>\n<p><strong>Common Ground:</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<h2>Most Divisive Text</h2>\n<p><strong>Consensus Score:</strong> 34.13</p>\n<pre><code>The government should implement a transparent, revenue-neutral carbon fee that returns all proceeds directly to households as dividends, ensuring that polluters pay while protecting American families from rising costs. This market-based framework, supported by border adjustments to maintain international competitiveness, will drive private-sector innovation in clean energy and infrastructure without increasing the national debt or expanding the federal bureaucracy.\n</code></pre>\n<p><strong>Points of Contention:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>evaluation failed: no response</li>\n<li>bureaucratic creep: even if the text says &quot;without expanding the federal bureaucracy,&quot; the mechanism to collect fees and distribute dividends to every household would likely require a significant administrative apparatus.</li>\n<li>energy costs: even with a dividend, the immediate increase in the price of gas and electricity could hurt small businesses and the manufacturing sector.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>Detailed analysis: <a href='fileIndex/G-20260115-wGrf/political_optimization_20260115140206.md' target='_blank'>fileIndex/G-20260115-wGrf/political_optimization_20260115140206.md</a> <a href='fileIndex/G-20260115-wGrf/political_optimization_20260115140206.html' target='_blank'>html</a> <a href='fileIndex/G-20260115-wGr